      "review.rytr.faq3.answer": "The free plan provides 2,000 words per month indefinitely and includes access to all 30+ tools and templates. This is enough for creating social media posts, product descriptions, or testing different types of copy. It's not time-limited, making it genuinely useful for light users or those wanting to thoroughly test the platform.",
      "review.rytr.faq3.question": "Is the free plan actually useful or just a trial?",
      "review.rytr.faq4.answer": "Rytr can generate SEO-friendly content including meta descriptions, blog outlines, and keyword-rich copy. However, it doesn't include built-in SEO analysis tools like keyword research or content scoring. You'll need to use separate SEO tools to optimize and analyze the content Rytr generates.",
      "review.rytr.faq4.question": "Can Rytr help with SEO content?",
      "review.rytr.faq5.answer": "Rytr generates grammatically correct and coherent content, but it requires human review and editing. The AI excels at creating first drafts and overcoming writer's block, but you should always fact-check claims, verify information, and refine the output to match your specific needs and voice perfectly.",
      "review.rytr.faq5.question": "How accurate is the AI-generated content?",
      "review.rytr.faq6.answer": "Yes, all content generated with Rytr is yours to use commercially. You own the rights to the output and can use it for marketing, sales, advertising, client work, or any other business purpose. However, always review and edit the content to ensure it meets your quality standards and brand guidelines.",
      "review.rytr.faq6.question": "Can I use Rytr content commercially?",
